<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/16th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Riechenberg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1552">1552</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of Riechenberg was the settlement of 1552 by which the imperial city of Goslar submitted to Duke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-v-duke-of-brunswick-luneburg">Henry the Younger</a> of Brunswick-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wolfenbuttel">Wolfenbüttel</a> after years of conflict over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rammelsberg">Rammelsberg</a>. The city lost control of the mines and its forests to the duke, which began its long economic decline.</p></div>
